Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Hello,

I'm trying out the useful new geom_label geom in ggplot2 1.0.1.9003. I would like to remove the border from the labels or at least make it much thinner. Using the size or colour arguments to geom_label won't work because it also controls the text. I'm not sure which theme element the border of geom_label inherits from but I tried changing the line and rect. These had no effect on the label.

I can get what I want using geom_label(colour = NA) + geom_text() but it seems a bit hacky to me. I also can't see how it would work if I wanted a thinner line rather than no line. Is there a better way?

SessionInfo and lame example code at the end.

Thanks for reading,

Tom

library(ggplot2)

data(iris)

g <- ggplot(iris, aes(x = Sepal.Length, y = Sepal.Width, label = Species)) +
  geom_point()

# default plot
g + geom_label()

# removes text as well as border
g + geom_label(colour = NA)

# makes text too small
g + geom_label(size = 1)

# doesn't do anything to labels
g + geom_label() +
  theme(rect = element_rect(size = 0),
        line = element_line(size = 0))

# gets me what I want
g + geom_label(colour = NA) +
  geom_text()

